Description:
Proger is a global reality that brings together the best of Italian management, engineering and security expertise. A unique partner for public and private clients, able to guarantee the sustainability, development and execution of large-scale multidisciplinary projects.


With more than 70 years' experience, the company is now the leading independent engineering firm in Italy and is firmly established in the world rankings of international companies in the sector, compiled by Engineering News Record.


In Italy, it is responsible for the safety checks of over 7,000 works on the motorway network and is involved in the design of many of the country's largest infrastructure projects. On a national and international level, it is a key player in major urban, social and health development projects and plays a leading role in the energy transition, building renewable energy power plants, hydrogen plants and electrical and thermal energy storage systems.


Proger is present in Europe, Central Asia, Africa and the Middle East with hundreds of professionals who work with sensitivity to the territory and the social fabric to face new and increasingly global challenges with the utmost respect for the local context.


Proger's selection process ensures equal opportunities for all candidates and the transparency and homogeneity of the assessment criteria. Proger is committed to attracting and recruiting people with diverse backgrounds and abilities, and to pursuing gender equality in selection and recruitment.


Experience, skills and competencies are the guidelines for selecting our best candidates. Would you like to join our team?


Position:


The Senior ICT Engineer is responsible for the design, start-up and coordination of ICT services in the context of new projects and orders, acting as the main technical reference towards the customer and project stakeholders.


The figure oversees the entire start-up cycle of IT services, from the collection and analysis of requirements to the definition of architecture and services, from the coordination of suppliers and partners to the end of the project.


The aim is to ensure that ICT infrastructures and services are implemented in compliance with contractual requirements, company standards, agreed service levels and cybersecurity requirements.


Requirements:



* Manage the technical relationship with the customer for all aspects related to ICT services.
* Analyze the contractual scope and translate customer requirements into IT solutions and services.
* Collect, analyze and formalize technical, operational and safety requirements.
* Define the ICT architecture necessary for the launch of new projects, offices or operational headquarters.
* Coordinate the implementation and commissioning of ICT services up to go-live.
* Coordinate suppliers, system integrators, telecom providers and technology partners involved in the project.
* Verify the progress of activities against agreed time, costs, technical requirements and service levels.
* Prepare and keep updated the technical and operational documentation of the project.

**Technical knowledge**
The role requires technical knowledge and design experience across ICT infrastructure, platforms and services. The required areas are listed below:



* network infrastructure;
* physical and virtual servers;
* Microsoft Server and Linux environments;
* Active Directory, Microsoft Entra ID and identity management;
* Microsoft 365;
* cloud services;
* virtualization;
* backup and disaster recovery systems;
* endpoint management and workstation management;
* endpoint security;
* ticketing systems and IT Service Management;
* cybersecurity and access management;
* collaboration and communication services;
* voice and VoIP systems.

The candidate must also be able to:



* define an operational plan for the launch of ICT services;
* coordinating internal and external technical teams;
* monitor KPIs and SLAs of services;
* support the definition of operating procedures and support models.
* understand customer needs and transform them into technical requirements;
* manage technical meetings and project progress;
* coordinating the resolution of problems by involving specialists and suppliers;
* prepare technical documentation, reports and presentations;

**Education And Experience**
Degree in computer science, engineering, telecommunications or equivalent professional experience.



* At least 12 years of experience in the ICT field.
* Experience in starting or managing IT infrastructures and services.
* Experience in the technical management of ICT projects.
* Direct experience in the relationship with customers and stakeholders.
* Experience in coordinating suppliers and technology partners.
* Experience in managing distributed or multi-site infrastructures.
* Experience in international contexts and complex projects is preferred.

**Personal Skills**

* Strong customer orientation.
* Excellent interpersonal and communication skills.
* Technical leadership.
* Ability to coordinate multidisciplinary teams.
* Problem solving and decision-making skills.
* Ability to work towards priorities and goals.
* Autonomy in the management of activities.
* Ability to operate in international and multicultural contexts.
* Ability to interface effectively with management, customer, technical teams and suppliers.
* Excellent English language both written and spoken.

***Are you a Registered Nurse with two (2) years of experience looking to make a difference in the lives of children and their families in Connecticut? If so, we invite you to take this opportunity to join our team at John Dempsey Hospital!***



The State of Connecticut, including the partnership between the Department of Children and Families (DCF) and UConn Health is currently recruiting for multiple second shift **Head Nurse** positions at John Dempsey Hospital, Solnit South Campus located in Middletown, CT.



**Position Highlights:**

**PCN 114011:**

* Location: Acadia Unit, Middletown, CT
* Full-time | 40 Hours per week
* 2nd Shift | 2:45 pm – 11:15 pm
* Days Off Per Pay Period:
* Week One: Saturday, Sunday, Thursday
* Week Two: Wednesday

**PCN 134998:**

* Location: Manhasset Unit, Middletown, CT
* Full-time | 40 Hours per week
* 2nd Shift | 2:45 pm – 11:15 pm
* Days Off Per Pay Period:
* Week One: Friday, Monday
* Week Two: Saturday, Sunday

**PCN 134999:**

* Location: Passaic Unit, Middletown, CT
* Full-time | 40 Hours per week
* 2nd Shift | 2:45 pm – 11:15 pm
* Days Off Per Pay Period:
* Week One: Friday, Monday
* Week Two: Saturday, Sunday

**The Role:**

Are you an experienced nursing professional ready to take on a leadership role while making a meaningful difference in the lives of children and families? We are seeking dedicated and compassionate Head Nurses to lead nursing operations and provide high-quality, individualized care to those we serve.



In this vital role, you will lead professional and paraprofessional nursing staff, coordinate unit workflow, establish priorities, oversee assignments, and promote high standards of nursing practice. You will also play a key role in staff development by providing training, guidance, and clinical direction while supporting the delivery of safe, effective, and consistent care.



As a **Head Nurse**, you will remain engaged in direct clinical care by conducting comprehensive nursing assessments, developing and evaluating health care plans, managing an assigned caseload, providing nursing consultation, and collaborating with interdisciplinary teams to promote continuity of care. You will also help ensure compliance with applicable regulations and standards, oversee the safe management of medications and controlled substances, and respond to emergencies as needed.



**About John Dempsey Hospital (JDH):**

JDH is widely recognized as a center of excellence for family-centered treatment of children and youth with serious emotional disturbances. This state-administered Psychiatric facility and hospital provides comprehensive care to children and adolescents under the age of eighteen, with severe mental illness and related behavioral and emotional problems who cannot be safely assessed or treated in a less restrictive setting.



**New!** Connecticut has joined the Nurse Licensure Compact effective October 1, 2025. Visit **Nurse Licensure Compact** for more details.



**What’s In It For You:**

Visit our **new** State Employee Benefits Overview page!

* Professional growth and paid professional development opportunities.
* A healthy work-life balance to all employees.
* State of Connecticut is an eligible Public Service Loan Forgiveness employer, meaning you may be eligible to have qualifying student loan forgiveness after 10 years of service. Click here for more information.

**Discover the opportunity to:**

* Engage in a rewarding career
* Assist our employees so they can achieve success
* Make a difference in the public sector
* Work together in a collaborative team environment

**If you are a confident nursing leader who is passionate about quality care, staff development, teamwork, and improving outcomes for children and families, we encourage you to bring your expertise to DCF and make an ImpaCT! Apply today and become part of a team dedicated to strengthening families and creating brighter futures.**






**Selection Plan**
------------------

